Files copied from gmp-6.3.0/: mini-gmp/mini-gmp.c, mini-gmp/mini-gmp.h,
mini-gmp/README, COPYINGv2, COPYINGv3, COPYING.LESSERv3; all unchanged
but one change to mini-gmp.c, marked MERI there.

The change: where the compiler has an unsigned type of 128 bits
(__SIZEOF_INT128__), gmp_umul_ppmm multiplies two limbs with it, one
multiplication of the CPU instead of four of their halves; elsewhere the
macro is the original. mpn_mul_1, mpn_addmul_1, mpn_submul_1 and the
division by an inverse use it: pidigits runs in about half the time. The
difference from gmp-6.3.0/mini-gmp/mini-gmp.c:

133a134,143
> /* MERI: where the compiler has a type of 128 bits, one multiplication
>    of the CPU for two limbs, not four of their halves (PROVENANCE) */
> #if defined(__SIZEOF_INT128__)
> #define gmp_umul_ppmm(w1, w0, u, v)					\
>   do {									\
>     unsigned __int128 __ww = (unsigned __int128) (u) * (v);		\
>     w0 = (mp_limb_t) __ww;						\
>     w1 = (mp_limb_t) (__ww >> GMP_LIMB_BITS);				\
>   } while (0)
> #else
173a184
> #endif /* MERI */

